IDEA PIN (T8) — DESIGN-GATED (2026-07-05 sweep): `! ?persist`
optional-arm DI needs the T8 firing-granularity ruling (per-write?
batch?) AND the connection-purity resolution (a handler holding a live
conn vs transplant purity — the ORM-showcase collision). Optional-arm
machinery exists (400_144); the store-side semantics are the open half.
Not machinery-cheap; needs the walk.


---

RULED 2026-10-24 — firing granularity settled: an installed `! ?persist`
arm fires ONCE PER APPLY, payload shaped like the write. A batch apply is
one firing carrying the plural delta; scalar writes degenerate to today's
per-write shape. Same law as 690_019/690_020 — the apply is the atomicity
unit; per-row observation would fabricate states that never existed.

STILL OPEN: (a) connection purity — may the handler hold a live connection
across the apply (the ORM-showcase collision; lean: no, the arm receives
the delta and initiates its own IO — unresolved); (b) install surface —
arms on `watch`? on `link`? — do not invent in a test. (c) deferred with
690_019: granularity override via annotation (binding-annotation lane a
candidate).
